@@ -9246,3 +9246,4 @@ Did NOT modify research-roadmap.yaml or scripts/research_conductor.py. Did NOT p
 - 2026-06-17: PHASE D (CONTINUOUS SELF-LEARNING -- the mandated self-learning experiment; NEW mechanism = a LEARNED FRAME ENCODER) -- does a LEARNED frame encoder (vs the GENERIC grid features that nulled in exp4318) carry a game-invariant progress signal that transfers cross-game? .399 (exp4318) PROVED generic grid features (nonzero/colors/objects/spread/dominant) do NOT transfer cross-game (reduction ~1.0, positive control passed) and LOGGED a 'game-invariant ARC value representation' gap. research-program.md mandates >=1 self-learning experiment/milestone; re-measuring generic-feature transfer is churn. The NEW mechanism (the gap's candidate fix): train a small LEARNED frame ENCODER (a tiny CNN / learned feature map over raw frames, CPU) on the now-11 reproducibly-solved games' traces, producing a learned embedding the value-head consumes; re-test LEAVE-ONE-GAME-OUT cross-game search-efficiency transfer (does the learned-encoder value-head reduce OfflineSolver search states on a held-out game vs an untrained/uniform heuristic?). POSITIVE CONTROL: confirm the baseline solver solves the held-out level (FALSE_NEGATIVE_RISK guard). Report cross_game_state_reduction (held-out states_uniform / states_transferred) + per-held-out-game reads + a bootstrap CI95. Emit learned_encoder_transfer_helps BARE bool := (reduction > 1.0 AND CI95 lower bound > 1.0). verifier_is_oracle=false. A learned-encoder transfer where generic features failed CLOSES the gap (a richer game-invariant representation); a powered null SHARPENS the gap (the representation is still insufficient -> more solved games or a different encoder) and is decision-grade. NO TRM training; NO LLM weight mutation (the encoder + value-head are a tiny CPU heuristic over solver state). (⚠️ Research Finding) — honest_verdict=complete: learned_frame_encoder_transfer_no_improvement_positive_control_passed; results/experiment_4331_self_learning_learned_frame_encoder_cross_game_transfer.json
 - 2026-06-17: PHASE E1 (SOTA-ingestion; mandatory per SOTA-Ingestion Cycle Discipline) -- ingest the SOTA for the .400 bleeding-edge forks (scaled external-verifier-guided DiffusionGemma generation, executable-world-model ARC solving, learned-frame-encoder cross-game transfer) and MAP the strongest 3-5 methods onto the .401 roadmap conditioned on the .400 outcomes (did the in-generation moat REPLICATE on a 2nd corpus / did the adaptive scale-up beat its control? did E3 land a deep-tail solve? did the learned encoder transfer?). Use the RELIABLE channel ONLY (scripts/sweep_clusters.py / sweep_semscholar.py + low-concurrency WebSearch/WebFetch) -- /deep-research is BANNED in-loop. Every method MUST carry a real arXiv ID/URL (VERIFY each). Update research-studying.md (mark ingested) and emit flagged_for_v401. (✅ Complete) — honest_verdict=complete: sota_ingestion_v401_mapped; results/experiment_4332_sota_ingestion_v401.json
 - 2026-06-17: PHASE E2 (hygiene; per Missing-Verifier Gap Logging + registry hygiene) -- reconcile the verifier registry + gaps to .400 truth, run the GAP-4 execution regression guard, and LOG missing-verifier gaps. Record the .400 outcomes: the in-generation moat replication (exp4325 in_generation_moat_replicates + controls_differentiated), the adaptive scale-up (exp4326 adaptive_guidance_beats_control + domain_used), the E3 deep-tail solves (exp4327/4328/4329 offline_reproduced + verifier_accuracy_per_round + any missing-world-model-rule gaps), the shallow-tail sweep (exp4330 reproducible_total_levels + tn36_schema_finding), the learned-encoder cross-game transfer (exp4331 learned_encoder_transfer_helps). Update ops/verifier_registry.yaml + ops/verifier_gaps.md (e.g. close/sharpen the 'game-invariant ARC value representation' gap per exp4331; log any missing-world-model-rule gaps from E3; the ARC-grid-generation-scorer gap if exp4326's adaptive arm stayed open). Run the GAP-4 execution regression guard (no regression vs .399). Use the robust aggregate-available helper (read available artifacts, report gaps -- do NOT hard-block all-False if one is missing). Emit regression_guard_passed BARE bool. (⚠️ Research Finding) — honest_verdict=complete: registry_gaps_manifest_reconciled_to_v400_truth_regression_guard_passed_True_gaps_logged_7_robust_aggregator_used; results/experiment_4333_verifier_registry_gaps_hygiene.json
+- 2026-06-17: PHASE E3 (hardware continuity; opportunistic per north-star §3) -- KV260 terminal/opportunistic (SSH-only reachability + xmutil listapps; NO host SD-card precondition), PolarFire CPU dispatch hash-verify, GateMate USB detect (`openFPGALoader -c dirtyJtag --detect`). KV260 is terminal (north-star §3) so the per-board mandate relaxes to opportunistic; this task keeps the boards visible without blocking the milestone. Report per-board reachability + any opportunistic result. NO board blocks the milestone (honest blocked_<board> per board is fine). (⚠️ Blocked) — honest_verdict=complete: hardware_continuity_4334_kv260_kv260_terminal_xmutil_listapps_blocked_returncode_1_polarfire_polarfire_hash_verified_cpu_dispatch_succeeded_gatemate_blocked_gatemate_unreachable_ssh_usb_reachability_only; results/experiment_4334_hardware_continuity.json
